  "limitations": [
    "Inputs are frozen caller-supplied snapshots; collection across live browser stores and discovery of omitted journals are not automatic.",
    "Recovery retains burned allocation floors and completed address/exposure inventory, but not allocator request IDs or pending search work.",
    "The caller must retain prior payment exposures when successor allocation journals were initialized from an older backup; inventory carry-forward is separate work.",
    "Current balances, UTXOs, canonical replay and inclusion are omitted and require fresh observation.",
    "Existing live account/Qi journals have explicit monotonic merge APIs; coordinated live restore across all types is separate work.",
    "The existing 16-origin, 64-scope, 100000-record and 16 MiB full-backup limits apply, plus 128 journal descriptors totaling 16 MiB public state.",
    "Fuzz capture covers account, Qi and payment journals with fixed public toy proofs; mixed-journal collisions and HD capture are deterministic tests.",
    "Bounded 65536-byte sanitizer fuzz input; no attacker-selected password KDF, sustained-fuzz claim or LeakSanitizer claim.",
    "No public-network transactions or real funds used."
  ],
